## Summary

ConfidentialMPTSend missing checkExtraFeatures for sfCredentialIDs.

## Details

ConfidentialMPTSend does not implement checkExtraFeatures to gate the sfCredentialIDs field on the featureCredentials amendment. All other transactors that accept sfCredentialIDs (Payment, EscrowFinish, PaymentChannelClaim, AccountDelete) properly implement checkExtraFeatures to reject the field when featureCredentials is not enabled. ConfidentialMPTSend only checks featureConfidentialTransfer in its preflight, but never gates sfCredentialIDs on featureCredentials.

**Root cause**: ConfidentialMPTSend.cpp lacks a checkExtraFeatures override that checks for ctx.tx.isFieldPresent(sfCredentialIDs) && !ctx.rules.enabled(featureCredentials). The ConfidentialMPTSend.h header also doesn't declare this override.

`src/libxrpl/tx/transactors/token/ConfidentialMPTSend.cpp:14-65`
```cpp
NotTEC
ConfidentialMPTSend::preflight(PreflightContext const& ctx)
{
    if (!ctx.rules.enabled(featureConfidentialTransfer))
        return temDISABLED;
    // ... no checkExtraFeatures override exists
    if (auto const err = credentials::checkFields(ctx.tx, ctx.j); !isTesSuccess(err))
        return err;
    return tesSUCCESS;
}
```

**Exploit scenario**: If featureConfidentialTransfer is activated before featureCredentials (unlikely but theoretically possible with independent amendment voting), an attacker could submit a ConfidentialMPTSend transaction with sfCredentialIDs that passes preflight validation (credentials::checkFields only checks format). The transaction would fail in preclaim (credentials::valid would find no credential objects exist since CredentialCreate requires the amendment), but it would bypass the early rejection that other transactors provide. This wastes network resources by allowing malformed transactions further into the pipeline.

**Financial impact**: No direct financial impact - transactions fail in preclaim. Defense-in-depth gap only.

**Invariant gap**: No invariant checker covers amendment gating. This is a preflight/structural validation gap.

**Suggested fix**: Add a checkExtraFeatures override to ConfidentialMPTSend that returns false when sfCredentialIDs is present and featureCredentials is not enabled, matching the pattern used by Payment, EscrowFinish, PaymentChannelClaim, and AccountDelete.

